C# File Operations & Data Management
1. Creating & Writing File
Initializes a new text file named Index.txt and uses StreamWriter to write initial text lines (Welcome Jamhuuriya, Welcome CA244, computer application) into the file before safely closing the stream.   
creating file and processing and close.png

2. Reading & Populating ListBox
Checks whether Index.txt exists, reads all text lines at once into an array using File.ReadAllLines(), clears listBox1, and iterates through the lines to display them in the user interface.

3. Deleting Selected Item & Syncing File
Verifies that an item is selected (SelectedIndex != -1), removes the chosen item from listBox1, recreates Index.txt using File.CreateText(), and rewrites the remaining items back into the file to keep local storage synchronized.

4. Deleting Entire File & Resetting UI
Checks for the existence of Index.txt, completely deletes the physical file from disk using File.Delete(), clears all items from listBox1, and notifies the user with a MessageBox.   
delete file.png


5. Exception & Error Handling
Encloses all file operations within try-catch blocks to capture unexpected runtime errors (such as missing path references or file lock issues) and displays clear error details via MessageBox.Show().   
delete file.png
